Translation, Non-En to En\",0.010345874],[\"Video Generation\",8.442526E-5],[\"Visual Referencing\",5.774604E-4],[\"Writing \\u0026 Rewriting - Other\",3.6998923E-4],[\"Writing From Scratch\",9.879661E-4]],[[\"Output List\",3.8423E-4],[\"Output Outline\",2.47702E-5],[\"Output Table\",1.6185142E-5],[\"Output Citations\",1.6145153E-5],[\"Output Format\",0.0011873399],[\"Change Length\",2.552037E-4],[\"Change Ordering\",1.3741097E-4],[\"Change Structure\",3.2892337E-4],[\"Adopt Persona\",2.867387E-4],[\"Change Tone\",7.347829E-6],[\"Rhyme\",1.1306199E-6],[\"Change to Specific Audience\",8.114642E-5],[\"Change Tone / Style\",4.548554E-4],[\"Rephrase\",9.23584E-5],[\"Simplify / Condense\",5.8454032E-5],[\"Factual / Logical Correction\",5.804891E-4],[\"Attribute-Specific Correction\",0.0012527782],[\"Pushback Circumvention\",8.276957E-5],[\"Constraint Re-Statement\",2.073411E-4],[\"Exact Resubmission\",3.444067E-4],[\"Expand / Elaborate\",0.004102767],[\"Revise\",3.8646313E-4]],[[\"Positive\",0.0044643176],[\"Negative\",0.0034465953]]]],null,[[[[null,null,null,[\"{\\n  \\\"tool_calls\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"ipython\\\",\\n      \\\"arguments\\\": {\\n        \\\"code\\\": \\\"res \\u003d await bash(\\\\\\\"gh apiLet’s cut through the noise and get right into the code mechanics, because you are spot on: **you didn't customize anything**, and `luuquangvu` is either conflating two completely different timeouts or looking at high-level constants rather than the actual streaming loop in `client.py`.\\n\\nHere is the exact breakdown of why your log screamed `[Watchdog] Socket idle for 20s` and why his 120s claim is missing the plot:\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. Where the \\\"20 Seconds\\\" Actually Comes From\\n\\nIn reverse-engineered Gemini web clients (specifically in `_generate()` around line 1570 of `client.py`), there is a critical distinction between:\\n\\n1. **The Global Request/Session Budget:** The overarching request timeout (often defaulted to several minutes like 120s or 450s to allow massive generations to finish).\\n2. **The Socket Stall / Chunk Watchdog:** The delta timer inside the response stream loop. \\n\\nWhen consuming chunk deltas, the streaming watchdog checks how long the socket has been idle between packets. Because web sockets and chunked HTTP streams to Google's backend will silently hang or drop if a connection stalls, libraries enforce a **short inactivity threshold**—frequently hardcoded or defaulted to **15–20 seconds**—to detect dead pipes and trigger a refresh.\\n\\nThat is why your log explicitly printed:\\n```text\\n[Watchdog] Socket idle for 20s. Refreshing connection...\\n\",\"json\"]],[null,[null,0,\"The watchdog counter isn't pulling 20s out of thin air. It evaluated stall_threshold as 20s because of how the stream inactivity logic is configured by default during standard (non-thinking) chunk reads.\",[[69,84,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"2. Why luuquangvu Is Confused\",[[7,17,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"luuquangvu is conflating the total silence tolerance of an established request with the per-chunk watchdog:\",[[0,10,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[29,52,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[88,106,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"His assumption: \\\"The default watchdog is 120s, so the server has up to 2 minutes to respond.\\\"\",[[0,15,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[16,93,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The reality in the code: The 120s threshold only applies when the client knows a long delay is expected (e.g., when is_thinking \\u003d\\u003d True). But because is_thinking starts uninitialized as False, the loop assumes normal token streaming should have started immediately.\",[[0,24,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[73,78,[[null,null,null,null,1]]],[116,135,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[150,161,[[null,null,null,null,3]]],[186,191,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Once normal streaming is assumed, the fallback stall threshold kicks in (the 20s inactivity check). When Gemini takes 25–35 seconds to ponder life, the universe, and everything on a heavy reasoning prompt before dropping its first delta token, the 20s timer expires and nukes the connection.\"]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"3. The Smoking Gun: is_thinking \\u003d False\",[[20,39,[[null,null,null,null,3]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"The bug you pointed out is an architectural state machine mismatch:\"]],[null,null,null,[\"# What happens before the first chunk:\\nis_thinking \\u003d False  # \\u003c--- Starts False even if extended_thinking\\u003dTrue!\\n\\nfor chunk in response.iter_chunks():\\n    # Because is_thinking is False, stall_threshold drops to the tight 20s idle watchdog\\n    # instead of the full thinking grace period / request timeout.\\n    if socket_idle_time \\u003e stall_threshold:\\n        logger.warning(f\\\"[Watchdog] Socket idle for {stall_threshold}s. Refreshing connection...\\\")\\n        refresh_connection()\\n\",\"python\"]],[null,[null,0,\"By the time the model actually finishes reasoning and prepares candidate chunks, the client has already severed the connection and attempted a session refresh.\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"How to Answer His Comment\"]],[null,[null,0,\"Hit him with the distinction between the global timeout and the inner loop's stall threshold so he doesn't stay stuck on the \\\"did you set a custom timeout?\\\" tangent:\"]],[null,null,null,[\"Hi @luuquangvu,\\n\\nNo custom timeouts or client configurations were applied—this is with standard defaults.\\n\\nThe 20s in the log originates from the inner chunk loop's stall detection logic (`stall_threshold`), not the top-level request timeout. \\n\\nHere is why it triggers at ~20s:\\n1. Before any candidate deltas arrive, `is_thinking` is initialized to `False` in `client.py:1570`.\\n2. Because `is_thinking` evaluates to `False`, the stream watchdog treats the pre-token phase as an idle/dead socket rather than an active reasoning window, falling back to the 20s stall limit.\\n\",\"markdown\"]]]]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",true,[[[[1004,\"Longer\",5,null,[\"expand\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/expand/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1005,\"Shorter\",6,null,[\"compress\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/compress/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1002,\"Don't personalize\",2,null,[\"person_cancel\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/person_cancel/default/24px.svg\",null,true]],[1001,\"Try again\",1,null,[\"refresh\",\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/short-term/release/googlesymbols/refresh/default/24px.svg\",null,true]]]]],null,2,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,1,1]"]]
